      "target_paragraph_end": null,
      "author_tier": "practitioner",
      "author_id": "user_local",
      "author_name": "NC",
      "author_role": "Practitioner",
      "title": "Second/Subseuqnet offences",
      "body_markdown": "Issue of whether a person is sentenced as first or second/subsequent offence is defined at section 9. Typically sentencing of multiple offences where no prior relevant conviction, all offences would be sentenced as first offences (albeit with aggravation). This is still preferable for defendants than where sentencing occurs on separate days as the subsequent convictions are sentenced as 2nd.",
      "body_html": "<p>Issue of whether a person is sentenced as first or second/subsequent offence is defined at section 9. Typically sentencing of multiple offences where no prior relevant conviction, all offences would be sentenced as first offences (albeit with aggravation). This is still preferable for defendants than where sentencing occurs on separate days as the subsequent convictions are sentenced as 2nd.</p>",
      "visibility": "public",
      "status": "active",
      "version": 1,
      "created_at": "2026-10-01 03:19:27",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-01 03:19:27"
    },
